{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-103952",
  "enisaUuid": "f41e2fc6-97f8-3167-99e7-d16d538a81c7",
  "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: handle empty FILS association request payload\n\nfils_encrypt_assoc_req() accepts a (Re)Association Request frame whose\nlast element is the FILS Session element.  crypt_len is then zero and\naes_siv_encrypt() is called with an empty plaintext.\n\nkmemdup() returns ZERO_SIZE_PTR for a zero-length allocation, so the\nunconditional sg_init_one() puts an invalid page into the scatterlist.\nWith CONFIG_DEBUG_SG this triggers a kernel BUG in sg_set_buf();\nwithout the debug check the bogus page is handed to the crypto backend.\n\nAES-SIV is defined for empty plaintext and the S2V result is then the\ncomplete output, so handle this case before the CTR step, which has\nnothing to encrypt.",
  "datePublished": "Oct 18, 2026, 3:46:23 PM",
  "dateUpdated": "Oct 30, 2026, 12:38:50 PM",
  "baseScore": 0.0,
  "references": "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/de3297c8e521c0b0ddc89ece6fee84e25da9ecf0\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ce70c87252a14020cb40032efe208efc6e61b1ee\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d8c5dbbf584a1baaa008988ac64dd4495f7086bd\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b1e4a7eeb6a301ee33bd318982927cbdbae9f36\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2f5b62f6534d336a62fdb9e88b186dd70b4323ef\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/452f1c9b76f7a122bbc4630b9691bda4809677c4\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/20f939b0c151d1d28e6b62a76b2454fa6fe877f2\nhttps://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5bfd4b0b40b79781d900cb2f7da0685070f53c67\n",
